<!--
  Canon in D
  Johann Pachelbel (about 1680). Public domain.
  D major (F sharp, C sharp), 4/4, quarter = 66, 9 bars (33 s).
  The first violin's tune, which is played over the ground bass D A B F# G D G A
  (D, A, Bm, F#m, G, D, G, A): its first three variations, then the first again, ending on D.
  Melody only. The eighth-note variation (bars 5-6) is an octave above the original, so every
  note fits E4-B5 (the C4-B5 window).

  bar | right hand                 | words
    1 | F#5 E5 D5 C#5              | variation 1
    2 | B4 A4 B4 C#5               |
    3 | D5 C#5 B4 A4               | variation 2
    4 | G4 F#4 G4 E4               |
    5 | D5 F#5 A5 G5 F#5 D5 F#5 E5 | variation 3, an octave up
    6 | D5 B4 D5 A5 G5 B5 A5 G5    |
    7 | F#5 E5 D5 C#5              | variation 1
    8 | B4 A4 B4 C#5               |
    9 | D5                         |
-->
